WEBVTT

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:08.404
Captain's Log, Stardate 54129.4.

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:11.273
lt's a bittersweet day
for the crew of Voyager.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:12.936
We've finally found a home

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:15.274
for some
of our most precious cargo.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:18.283
Thank you again for taking care
of them, Captain.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:19.579
We're very grateful.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.586
We're just glad
that Rebi and Azan will have

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.588
a chance to grow up
with their own people

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.318
and that you've been kind enough
to let Mezoti join them.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:30.693
You can still come with us.

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:33.164
And you can still
stay on Voyager.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:35.997
Adapting to your absence
will be difficult.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.662
l'll miss you, too.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.341
lt's time.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.934
l've been studying
all available data

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:48.480
relevant to this species,
as you recommended.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:50.482
Familiarizing yourself
with their culture

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.517
will help you adapt.

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:55.020
On Wysanti, it's customary
not to say good-bye,

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:57.783
but l think l prefer
the human way.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:24.142
Energize.

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:37.619
We should deactivate
the children's alcoves.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:38.959
Right now?

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:41.966
They're a drain
on Voyager's power reserves.

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:44.298
ls there a problem?

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:46.065
lt just seems like

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:50.108
an insufficient amount
of time has passed.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.678
You're having
an emotional response

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.610
to the children's departure.

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:55.613
They'll be fine.

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.513
We should be happy for them.

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:58.949
Seven?

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.610
Yes?

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:03.212
You're crying.

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:10.222
My ocular implant
must be malfunctioning.

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:02.200
Crying is nothing
to be ashamed of, Seven.

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:03.402
You should have seen me

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:06.241
the first time l heard
Puccini's Tosca in the holodeck.

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:09.338
l sobbed through
the entire third act.

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:11.178
You're a hologram.
You can't cry.

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:12.878
Ordinarily,
but Lieutenant Torres

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:14.749
enhanced
my emotional subroutines,

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:17.346
so l could truly appreciate
the performance.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:18.890
Then your reaction
was the result

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:20.458
of a technological enhancement,

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:24.257
just as mine was the result
of a technological malfunction.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:27.026
Saying good-bye to the children
was a traumatic experience.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.068
Crying was a normal response.

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:30.067
Except that l was

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:31.603
in complete control
of my emotions.

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:40.168
Hmm. lt seems
l owe you an apology.

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:42.510
According to this,
your tears were the result

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:44.743
of a glitch in your
primary cortical node.

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:47.285
Have you experienced any
other malfunctions lately?

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:49.651
Headache? Dizziness?
Diminished motor function?

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:50.950
No.

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:52.786
Really?

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.952
Then you won't mind if l check

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:58.621
the bio-monitors in your alcove
just to be sure?

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:01.064
l've experienced
an occasional headache.

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:02.499
Why didn't you come to see me?

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:04.593
The malfunctions have
not affected my work.

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:06.831
Seven, if you're
having problems,

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:09.066
you need to let me know.

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:11.143
lf it'll make you feel better,

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:13.439
l'll be more forthcoming
in the future.

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:15.105
You're all heart.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:17.775
l'll schedule
some follow-up tests

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.613
and make my report
to the Captain.

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:22.280
l'd prefer to keep this
between us.

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:24.255
l don't want
to worry the Captain.

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:26.986
We've always kept her informed
of your medical needs.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:30.086
lt was my understanding
that all members of this crew

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:32.893
have the right to doctor-patient
confidentiality.

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:36.594
lf you want to keep
this between us,

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:39.171
that's where it'll stay.

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:03.524
Have you finished charting
the nebula in Sector 949?

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:05.860
Several hours ago.

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:13.229
l've been thinking.

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:15.637
While l'm grateful
for the opportunity

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:17.403
to assist you in Astrometrics,

00:06:17.477 --> 00:06:20.446
l'd like to take on
more challenging assignments.

00:06:20.513 --> 00:06:22.845
l can assign you
additional diagnostics.

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:24.507
That's not what l meant.

00:06:24.584 --> 00:06:26.518
l want to work on the Bridge.

00:06:26.586 --> 00:06:28.884
You don't have
the proper training.

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:30.216
That's why l'd like to take

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:32.450
the entrance exam
for Starfleet Academy.

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:35.357
l could forward it to Earth

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:36.986
in the next
datastream transmission.

00:06:37.063 --> 00:06:38.894
lf l pass, l could take
the basic classes

00:06:38.998 --> 00:06:40.192
from Commander Tuvok.

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:42.894
He was an instructor
at the Academy.

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:45.698
Your plan is ambitious.

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:47.534
Then you think it's a good idea?

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:50.235
You could take
the classes with me.

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:53.073
Earn your own commission.

00:06:53.146 --> 00:06:54.477
l believe l've
already assimilated

00:06:54.547 --> 00:06:55.605
enough Starfleet training.

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:58.206
l'll need a letter of
recommendation from the Captain.

00:06:58.284 --> 00:07:00.309
l'll speak to her.

00:07:06.726 --> 00:07:08.819
l have work to complete
in the cargo bay.

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:10.019
Can you finish here?

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:11.825
Of course.

00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:27.771
Computer, initiate
regeneration cycle.

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:30.672
Unable to comply.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:31.808
Why?

00:07:31.884 --> 00:07:33.852
The interface is incompatible.

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:37.515
Run a diagnostic of Alcove 01.

00:07:38.858 --> 00:07:40.587
Diagnostic complete.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:44.619
Alcove 01 is operating
within normal parameters.

00:07:44.697 --> 00:07:48.155
lnitiate regeneration cycle.

00:07:49.569 --> 00:07:50.831
Unable to comply.

00:07:50.937 --> 00:07:52.029
Clarify.

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:55.130
Your cortical node
is malfunctioning.

00:08:05.017 --> 00:08:07.577
Seven. l didn't see you.

00:08:07.653 --> 00:08:09.712
l was just leaving.

00:08:09.789 --> 00:08:11.120
Before breakfast?

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:13.784
What time is it?

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.350
0500.

00:08:15.428 --> 00:08:19.057
Don't tell me you've
been here all night.

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:21.361
l was unable to regenerate.

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:23.435
Anything on your mind?

00:08:23.536 --> 00:08:27.233
My alcove is malfunctioning.

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:29.638
Well, you should ask B'Elanna
to take a look at it.

00:08:29.709 --> 00:08:30.869
l didn't want to wake her.

00:08:30.943 --> 00:08:33.275
What's all this?

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:35.871
Nutritional supplements.

00:08:35.982 --> 00:08:37.313
l thought they would compensate.

00:08:37.383 --> 00:08:39.510
Your own recipe?

00:08:39.585 --> 00:08:41.780
lt's a mixture
of metabolic enzymes

00:08:41.854 --> 00:08:43.151
and protein extract.

00:08:43.222 --> 00:08:45.281
Let me make you one
of my Talaxian omelets.

00:08:45.358 --> 00:08:48.486
lt may not have as many enzymes,
but it'll taste better.

00:08:48.561 --> 00:08:50.028
That won't be necessary.

00:08:50.096 --> 00:08:52.826
l think l'll take your advice
and wake Lieu...

00:08:52.899 --> 00:08:54.093
Lieutenant...

00:08:55.568 --> 00:08:56.899
Seven!

00:09:03.376 --> 00:09:04.468
Neelix to Sick Bay.

00:09:04.544 --> 00:09:05.636
Medical emergency.

00:09:18.991 --> 00:09:21.551
You lost consciousness
in the Mess Hall.

00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:27.593
Your body's begun
to reject your implants.

00:09:27.667 --> 00:09:30.033
l'm afraid it's a result
of that glitch we found

00:09:30.136 --> 00:09:31.194
in your cortical node.

00:09:31.304 --> 00:09:34.034
Apparently, it's more
serious than we thought.

00:09:37.176 --> 00:09:39.201
The node is destabilizing.

00:09:39.278 --> 00:09:42.270
lt's no longer able
to regulate your implants.

00:09:42.348 --> 00:09:44.509
They're shutting down
one by one.

00:09:45.618 --> 00:09:48.519
When you've disconnected
implants in the past,

00:09:48.588 --> 00:09:49.885
l've always adapted.

00:09:49.956 --> 00:09:51.981
Minor implants--

00:09:52.058 --> 00:09:53.753
an assimilation tubule here,

00:09:53.826 --> 00:09:55.316
a few nanoprobes there--

00:09:55.394 --> 00:09:57.885
nothing crucial
to your human physiology,

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:01.124
but these implants control
your vital functions.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.294
And without my cortical node
to regulate them, l'll die.

00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:05.665
Correct?

00:10:13.012 --> 00:10:15.378
Borg technology
is highly adaptive.

00:10:15.448 --> 00:10:18.576
My cortical node
will repair itself in time.

00:10:18.651 --> 00:10:19.811
l don't think so, Seven.

00:10:19.885 --> 00:10:22.251
lf anything, the deterioration
is accelerating.

00:10:22.321 --> 00:10:24.448
You'll have to stay here
for observation.

00:10:24.523 --> 00:10:27.151
l think l've been
sufficiently observed.

00:10:27.226 --> 00:10:29.194
Would you excuse us, please?

00:10:31.931 --> 00:10:33.558
l'm sorry for what's happening.

00:10:33.633 --> 00:10:35.533
You have every right
to be angry,

00:10:35.635 --> 00:10:38.365
but that isn't going to
help us solve this problem.

00:10:38.471 --> 00:10:40.336
The node will correct itself.

00:10:40.406 --> 00:10:41.532
Suppose it doesn't?

00:10:41.641 --> 00:10:43.370
For the sake of argument.

00:10:43.442 --> 00:10:46.104
ls it possible
to replicate a new one?

00:10:46.178 --> 00:10:48.373
The technology is too complex.

00:10:50.282 --> 00:10:51.840
What if this had happened

00:10:51.917 --> 00:10:54.385
when you were part
of the collective?

00:10:54.453 --> 00:10:57.820
How would the Borg have
repaired the damage?

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:00.051
They wouldn't have.

00:11:00.126 --> 00:11:03.721
Trying to repair a node
would be a futile exercise.

00:11:03.796 --> 00:11:06.162
The Borg would simply
replace it.

00:11:10.469 --> 00:11:13.461
Harry, we passed
a Borg debris field

00:11:13.572 --> 00:11:14.539
six or seven days ago

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:16.631
just outside
the Yontasa Expanse.

00:11:16.742 --> 00:11:18.471
See if you can find it
on long-range sensors.

00:11:18.544 --> 00:11:19.602
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:19.679 --> 00:11:22.147
lt's not every day
we go looking for the Borg.

00:11:22.214 --> 00:11:23.545
What's up?

00:11:23.616 --> 00:11:25.777
Seven needs a new cortical node.

00:11:25.851 --> 00:11:27.614
Captain, need l remind you

00:11:27.687 --> 00:11:30.588
the Borg often return
to salvage damaged cubes.

00:11:30.656 --> 00:11:32.419
lt's a risk l'm willing to take.

00:11:32.491 --> 00:11:34.356
l want to help Seven
as much as anyone,

00:11:34.427 --> 00:11:35.621
but if we're not careful,

00:11:35.695 --> 00:11:37.492
we'll all end up
with cortical nodes.

00:11:37.563 --> 00:11:39.463
That's why l'm taking
the Flyer alone.

00:11:39.532 --> 00:11:41.466
l've located the debris field.

00:11:41.567 --> 00:11:43.535
Transmit the coordinates
to the Flyer.

00:11:43.636 --> 00:11:45.228
You have the Bridge, Commander.

00:11:45.337 --> 00:11:46.565
With all due respect...

00:11:46.672 --> 00:11:48.697
the last time you took
the Delta Flyer

00:11:48.808 --> 00:11:49.866
to confront the Borg,

00:11:49.975 --> 00:11:52.205
it ended up
in a couple thousand pieces.

00:11:52.278 --> 00:11:54.803
l intend to bring it back
in one piece this time.

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:56.848
A good pilot might be
able to help you do that.

00:11:56.916 --> 00:11:58.781
Particularly if he's accompanied

00:11:58.851 --> 00:12:00.876
by an experienced
Tactical Officer.

00:12:00.953 --> 00:12:02.921
You shouldn't do this
by yourself, Captain.

00:12:05.791 --> 00:12:08.817
Well, then, gentlemen,
l guess you're with me.

00:12:17.269 --> 00:12:18.463
Captain.

00:12:18.571 --> 00:12:20.801
l'll meet you
in the Shuttle Bay.

00:12:20.873 --> 00:12:22.864
Have you talked to Seven?

00:12:22.975 --> 00:12:24.408
Just a few minutes ago.

00:12:24.477 --> 00:12:26.570
And you don't approve.

00:12:26.645 --> 00:12:27.942
Of what?

00:12:28.013 --> 00:12:29.207
My request.

00:12:29.281 --> 00:12:30.578
Request?

00:12:30.649 --> 00:12:33.140
l'm sure Seven will
discuss it with you

00:12:33.219 --> 00:12:34.777
when she has the chance.

00:12:34.854 --> 00:12:37.152
l'm sorry l bothered you.

00:12:37.223 --> 00:12:39.418
Obviously, no one's told you.

00:12:39.492 --> 00:12:41.084
Told me what?

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:42.787
Seven isn't well.

00:12:42.862 --> 00:12:45.490
What's wrong with her?

00:12:45.564 --> 00:12:47.498
Her cortical node is failing.

00:12:47.566 --> 00:12:48.965
Her cortical node?

00:12:49.101 --> 00:12:50.762
She's going to die.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:52.428
Not if we find a new node.

00:12:52.538 --> 00:12:55.473
We're on our way to search
a Borg debris field.

00:12:55.541 --> 00:12:57.805
l have experience
in Borg technology.

00:12:57.877 --> 00:12:59.208
Let me come with you.

00:12:59.278 --> 00:13:01.610
l appreciate the offer,
but it's too dangerous.

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:03.113
l'm willing to take the risk.

00:13:03.182 --> 00:13:04.547
l'm not willing to let you.

00:13:04.617 --> 00:13:07.381
l'll let you know how we did
as soon as we're back.

00:13:07.453 --> 00:13:08.943
Don't worry.

00:13:21.634 --> 00:13:22.896
Seven?

00:13:28.274 --> 00:13:29.673
Why are you here?

00:13:29.742 --> 00:13:31.937
The Captain told me
you were ill.

00:13:32.011 --> 00:13:33.137
l'm fine.

00:13:33.212 --> 00:13:34.702
Then why are you in Sick Bay?

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:36.077
That's not your concern.

00:13:36.148 --> 00:13:37.479
You have work to complete.

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:38.744
Report to Astrometrics.

00:13:38.818 --> 00:13:40.046
l've finished my work.

00:13:40.119 --> 00:13:41.552
Then l'll assign you more.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:43.451
ls there a problem?

00:13:43.522 --> 00:13:45.251
l wish to be alone.

00:13:45.324 --> 00:13:47.622
Come with me, please.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:56.625
Why is she so angry with me?

00:13:56.735 --> 00:13:58.532
She's not angry with you.

00:13:58.637 --> 00:13:59.865
She's just angry.

00:13:59.972 --> 00:14:01.371
l don't understand.

00:14:01.473 --> 00:14:03.839
lt's a common response
to serious illness.

00:14:03.909 --> 00:14:05.672
She's frustrated
to be confined,

00:14:05.744 --> 00:14:07.609
embarrassed
to appear vulnerable.

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:09.875
She shouldn't be
embarrassed in front of me.

00:14:09.949 --> 00:14:11.041
l'm her friend.

00:14:11.116 --> 00:14:12.549
And her pupil.

00:14:12.618 --> 00:14:14.779
She doesn't want you
or anyone else to see her

00:14:14.854 --> 00:14:16.116
when she's not at her best.

00:14:16.188 --> 00:14:17.621
lt's not her fault
that she's sick.

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:18.884
Of course not,

00:14:18.991 --> 00:14:21.289
but we have to allow
her to deal with this

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:22.292
in her own way...

00:14:22.361 --> 00:14:24.158
with as much dignity
as possible.

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:25.561
Give her time.

00:14:25.631 --> 00:14:26.996
She may decide

00:14:27.066 --> 00:14:28.897
she wants company,
and if she does,

00:14:29.068 --> 00:14:31.002
you're the first person
l'll call.

00:14:47.086 --> 00:14:48.485
l have isolated a section

00:14:48.554 --> 00:14:51.489
that contains the bodies
of approximately 37 drones.

00:14:51.557 --> 00:14:53.718
37 doesn't sound
approximate to me.

00:14:53.792 --> 00:14:56.420
These drones were killed
in an explosion.

00:14:56.495 --> 00:14:58.622
There are only a few
left intact.

00:14:58.697 --> 00:15:01.461
Looks like there's still a
breathable atmosphere inside.

00:15:01.533 --> 00:15:04.058
Any sign of active Borg ships
in the vicinity?

00:15:04.169 --> 00:15:05.659
Nothing on sensors.

00:15:05.771 --> 00:15:07.500
Huh.
That could change in a hurry.

00:15:07.606 --> 00:15:08.868
Run continuous scans.

00:15:08.974 --> 00:15:10.271
Yes, ma'am.

00:15:41.507 --> 00:15:42.474
Tuvok, here.

00:15:42.574 --> 00:15:45.008
Help me get this off him.

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:00.290
No apparent damage
to the cortical node.

00:16:47.172 --> 00:16:48.764
Captain, you've got company.

00:16:48.874 --> 00:16:51.843
There's a ship...

00:16:51.944 --> 00:16:55.038
Two to beam out.

00:16:55.114 --> 00:16:57.582
Delta Flyer, respond.

00:16:59.952 --> 00:17:02.921
Three humanoids have just
transported aboard this vessel.

00:17:03.022 --> 00:17:05.149
Drones?

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:07.681
The only drones here are dead...

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:09.489
and they belong to us.

00:17:12.498 --> 00:17:14.989
Who are you?

00:17:15.100 --> 00:17:17.330
Captain Kathryn Janeway
of the Starship Voyager.

00:17:17.436 --> 00:17:20.064
This is my debris field,
Captain.

00:17:20.172 --> 00:17:22.265
We weren't aware of that.

00:17:22.374 --> 00:17:24.535
What have you taken?

00:17:24.610 --> 00:17:25.872
A cortical node.

00:17:25.944 --> 00:17:27.673
We need it to save
one of my crew.

00:17:27.746 --> 00:17:30.874
Everything here belongs to us.

00:17:31.016 --> 00:17:33.883
Put down your weapons,
and l'll consider

00:17:33.952 --> 00:17:36.386
not activating
this laser scalpel.

00:17:59.011 --> 00:18:00.876
Sorry about the delay.

00:18:00.979 --> 00:18:04.005
They knocked
our transporters off-line.

00:18:15.861 --> 00:18:18.728
l need you at tactical!

00:18:18.797 --> 00:18:21.391
When l bring us around,
target their engine core.

00:18:21.467 --> 00:18:22.957
Aye, sir.

00:18:32.878 --> 00:18:35.005
Nice shot.

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:38.481
They're breaking pursuit.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.400
May l ask what you're doing?

00:18:57.503 --> 00:18:59.232
Your filing system
is inefficient.

00:18:59.338 --> 00:19:00.703
l'm implementing a new one.

00:19:00.806 --> 00:19:02.740
You should be in bed.

00:19:02.774 --> 00:19:04.708
Delivery for Seven of Nine.

00:19:04.776 --> 00:19:07.370
Tarcanian wildflowers.

00:19:07.446 --> 00:19:09.073
Cheery, don't you think?

00:19:10.282 --> 00:19:12.011
Ah. Well,
if you prefer gladiolas,

00:19:12.084 --> 00:19:14.211
l could go back
to the Airponics Bay.

00:19:14.286 --> 00:19:16.049
That won't be necessary,
Mr. Neelix.

00:19:16.121 --> 00:19:19.386
The flowers are lovely,
aren't they, Seven?

00:19:19.458 --> 00:19:20.823
Thank you.

00:19:20.959 --> 00:19:23.223
l'll admire them later.

00:19:23.295 --> 00:19:26.059
Actually, l thought
l'd stay and keep you company.

00:19:26.131 --> 00:19:30.568
Uh, Seven prefers not to
have visitors right now.

00:19:30.636 --> 00:19:33.230
Not even a visitor
with a Kadis-Kot board?

00:19:33.338 --> 00:19:34.305
Correct.

00:19:34.373 --> 00:19:35.840
But it's your favorite game.

00:19:35.974 --> 00:19:37.874
Personally...

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:40.444
l can't blame her.

00:19:40.512 --> 00:19:42.275
You're being
extremely insensitive.

00:19:42.347 --> 00:19:43.871
l am?

00:19:44.016 --> 00:19:47.042
You know perfectly very well
Seven is in a weakened state.

00:19:47.119 --> 00:19:49.451
She wouldn't stand
a chance against you.

00:19:49.521 --> 00:19:50.647
You're right.

00:19:50.722 --> 00:19:53.384
l-l don't know
what l was thinking.

00:19:53.458 --> 00:19:55.892
We'll play later
when you're feeling up to it.

00:19:55.994 --> 00:19:57.018
Green.

00:19:57.095 --> 00:19:59.359
l beg your pardon?

00:19:59.431 --> 00:20:01.126
l prefer the green pieces.

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:02.861
You'll use red.

00:20:02.968 --> 00:20:05.402
Doctor, do you think
she's up to it?

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:07.131
As long as you go easy on her.

00:20:07.239 --> 00:20:09.207
Janeway to the Doctor.

00:20:09.274 --> 00:20:10.536
Yes, Captain.

00:20:10.609 --> 00:20:13.169
We're back,
and we have the node.

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:37.896
l'm ready to disengage
the damaged node.

00:20:38.003 --> 00:20:41.530
Transfer Seven's cortical
functions to the computer.

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:43.107
Understood.

00:20:46.578 --> 00:20:48.170
Done.

00:20:48.247 --> 00:20:49.908
lnitiating the extraction.

00:21:04.696 --> 00:21:05.993
Vital functions are stable.

00:21:06.064 --> 00:21:07.531
-Time?
-20 seconds.

00:21:08.634 --> 00:21:10.067
Not yet.

00:21:10.135 --> 00:21:12.831
l have to realign
her primary neurodes first.

00:21:14.973 --> 00:21:17.669
The computer can't maintain her
cortical functions much longer.

00:21:18.744 --> 00:21:20.712
Ready.

00:21:29.655 --> 00:21:31.350
Her neural relays
are going to destabilize

00:21:31.423 --> 00:21:32.720
in ten seconds, nine...

00:21:32.791 --> 00:21:33.849
Almost finished.

00:21:33.925 --> 00:21:35.950
Eight, seven,

00:21:36.028 --> 00:21:38.496
six, five...

00:21:38.563 --> 00:21:41.327
Transfer Seven's cortical
functions to the new node.

00:21:45.237 --> 00:21:46.636
Something's wrong.

00:21:46.705 --> 00:21:48.332
She's going into
anaphylactic shock.

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:49.634
Her implants aren't adapting.

00:21:49.708 --> 00:21:51.005
They're rejecting the new node.

00:21:53.011 --> 00:21:54.273
She's losing synaptic cohesion.

00:21:54.346 --> 00:21:56.439
Apply a 20 millijoule
neurostatic pulse on my mark.

00:21:58.216 --> 00:21:59.478
Now.

00:22:03.155 --> 00:22:03.883
No effect.

00:22:03.955 --> 00:22:06.116
Again.

00:22:08.093 --> 00:22:10.391
lncrease the pulse.
30 millijoules.

00:22:18.637 --> 00:22:22.266
Computer, end simulation.

00:22:24.176 --> 00:22:25.143
Why did you stop?

00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:26.575
lt wasn't working.

00:22:26.645 --> 00:22:27.634
Run it again.

00:22:27.713 --> 00:22:29.840
Captain, this was
our 12th simulation.

00:22:29.915 --> 00:22:32.145
Something tells me 13
won't be our lucky number.

00:22:32.217 --> 00:22:35.812
The salvaged node has
been inactive too long.

00:22:35.887 --> 00:22:37.855
Then we'll find one that hasn't.

00:22:39.825 --> 00:22:41.816
No matter how many debris
fields we sift through,

00:22:41.893 --> 00:22:44.259
a node from a dead drone
isn't going to work.

00:22:44.329 --> 00:22:45.956
Who said anything
about a dead drone?

00:22:46.064 --> 00:22:47.224
What's that supposed to mean?

00:22:47.299 --> 00:22:48.857
We've infiltrated
Borg vessels before.

00:22:48.934 --> 00:22:50.424
lf that's what it's going
to take to save Seven,

00:22:50.535 --> 00:22:51.593
we'll do it again.

00:22:51.703 --> 00:22:53.671
Are you suggesting ending
one life to save another?

00:22:53.772 --> 00:22:54.966
l'm not giving up on her.

00:22:55.073 --> 00:22:57.303
Neither am l!

00:22:57.376 --> 00:22:59.344
l'll do everything
in my power to help her,

00:22:59.411 --> 00:23:01.402
but we both have
to face the possibility

00:23:01.513 --> 00:23:03.811
that it may not be enough.

00:23:10.655 --> 00:23:13.146
Red. Grid 13-3.

00:23:16.395 --> 00:23:18.488
They should've finished
the simulation by now.

00:23:18.563 --> 00:23:21.054
l'm sure they'll let you know
as soon as they do.

00:23:21.133 --> 00:23:22.566
Your move.

00:23:22.634 --> 00:23:25.194
Don't you have more
important duties to attend to?

00:23:25.303 --> 00:23:28.101
Nothing that can't wait.

00:23:28.173 --> 00:23:29.470
Despite
what the Doctor told you,

00:23:29.541 --> 00:23:30.530
l feel perfectly fine.

00:23:30.642 --> 00:23:31.631
Really?

00:23:31.743 --> 00:23:33.973
Because it looks to me
like you're about to lose.

00:23:38.750 --> 00:23:40.240
Kadis-Kot.

00:23:40.318 --> 00:23:42.582
l should've seen that coming.

00:23:42.654 --> 00:23:44.884
Oh, well, that makes what, uh,

00:23:44.956 --> 00:23:46.890
16 to 3, your lead?

00:23:46.958 --> 00:23:47.947
16 to 2.

00:23:48.026 --> 00:23:50.051
Oh, my mistake.

00:23:53.498 --> 00:23:55.898
Oh, uh...
well, l should really see

00:23:55.967 --> 00:23:58.765
how things are going
in the Mess Hall...

00:23:58.870 --> 00:24:01.896
but l'll be back later
for a rematch.

00:24:02.007 --> 00:24:03.338
Are you ready to proceed?

00:24:06.344 --> 00:24:07.641
According to the simulations,

00:24:07.712 --> 00:24:09.407
the salvaged node
isn't going to work.

00:24:09.481 --> 00:24:10.880
l'm sorry.

00:24:10.982 --> 00:24:13.712
l'm still researching
alternative treatments,

00:24:13.785 --> 00:24:17.414
and Harry and B'Elanna are going
to try to repair the faulty node

00:24:17.489 --> 00:24:19.116
using components
from your alcove.

00:24:19.191 --> 00:24:20.681
They'll fail.

00:24:23.895 --> 00:24:25.624
We're not giving up hope.

00:24:25.697 --> 00:24:27.358
Neither should you.

00:24:31.036 --> 00:24:31.900
With your permission,

00:24:32.037 --> 00:24:33.698
l'd like to return to my duties.

00:24:33.805 --> 00:24:34.897
That's not possible.

00:24:35.040 --> 00:24:36.337
l need to monitor
your condition.

00:24:36.408 --> 00:24:37.340
Captain?

00:24:37.409 --> 00:24:41.470
l'm afraid l have
to defer to the Doctor.

00:24:41.546 --> 00:24:45.380
lf you'd like, l can ask lcheb
to bring some of your work here.

00:25:09.307 --> 00:25:10.672
Doctor?

00:25:12.844 --> 00:25:14.209
Computer, locate the Doctor.

00:25:14.279 --> 00:25:15.837
The EMH is off-line.

00:25:15.914 --> 00:25:17.506
Activate the EMH.

00:25:19.451 --> 00:25:20.782
Doctor?

00:25:20.852 --> 00:25:21.876
l'm sorry, lcheb.

00:25:21.987 --> 00:25:23.477
l wasn't talking to you.

00:25:23.555 --> 00:25:24.579
Where's Seven?

00:25:24.656 --> 00:25:25.623
l wish l knew.

00:25:25.690 --> 00:25:26.884
When l refused to release her,

00:25:26.958 --> 00:25:29.324
she overrode my
autonomy protocols...

00:25:29.394 --> 00:25:31.658
in the middle of a sentence,
no less.

00:25:31.730 --> 00:25:34.130
Computer, locate Seven of Nine.

00:25:34.199 --> 00:25:36.531
Seven of Nine is in Sick Bay.

00:25:47.012 --> 00:25:49.071
He's looking for you...

00:25:49.147 --> 00:25:50.705
the Doctor.

00:25:51.816 --> 00:25:53.613
l ran into him in the corridor.

00:25:53.685 --> 00:25:57.883
He's about 30 seconds away
from calling a shipwide alert.

00:25:57.956 --> 00:26:00.447
Are you going to tell him
where l am?

00:26:00.525 --> 00:26:04.962
Nope. l know what it's like
to be stuck in Sick Bay.

00:26:05.030 --> 00:26:09.262
l've escaped the Doctor myself
once or twice.

00:26:09.367 --> 00:26:10.356
Thank you.

00:26:10.468 --> 00:26:11.526
Anytime.

00:26:13.805 --> 00:26:15.397
Lieutenant...

00:26:19.611 --> 00:26:21.772
when you die,

00:26:21.846 --> 00:26:25.373
do you believe your spirit
will go to Sto-Vo-Kor?.

00:26:25.450 --> 00:26:27.850
You shouldn't be thinking
about dying.

00:26:27.919 --> 00:26:29.682
According to the Doctor's
simulations,

00:26:29.754 --> 00:26:32.985
any attempt to adapt
the salvaged node will fail.

00:26:41.366 --> 00:26:44.460
Sto-Vo-Kor, Lieutenant...

00:26:44.569 --> 00:26:46.560
do you believe you'll go there?

00:26:46.671 --> 00:26:53.839
l guess it all depends
on how honorable my death is.

00:26:53.912 --> 00:26:57.348
But you do believe
there's something after death?

00:26:57.415 --> 00:26:59.940
l hope so.

00:27:06.057 --> 00:27:07.854
What about you?

00:27:10.095 --> 00:27:14.293
The Borg have no concept
of an afterlife.

00:27:14.366 --> 00:27:16.834
However, when a drone
is deactivated,

00:27:16.968 --> 00:27:19.163
its memories continue to reside

00:27:19.270 --> 00:27:21.636
in the collective's
consciousness.

00:27:21.706 --> 00:27:27.872
As long as the hive exists,
so will a part of that drone.

00:27:27.946 --> 00:27:31.438
You don't seem to take
much comfort in that.

00:27:32.517 --> 00:27:34.348
My link to the collective

00:27:34.419 --> 00:27:36.319
has been severed
for nearly four years.

00:27:38.390 --> 00:27:40.415
lf l die,

00:27:40.492 --> 00:27:42.585
everything that l've
accomplished in that time,

00:27:42.661 --> 00:27:45.528
everything l achieved
as an individual,

00:27:45.597 --> 00:27:47.531
will be lost.

00:27:47.599 --> 00:27:52.366
My memories, my experiences...

00:27:52.470 --> 00:27:56.099
it will be as if they...

00:27:56.207 --> 00:27:59.643
as if l never existed.

00:28:04.482 --> 00:28:07.645
l think you're
a little more memorable

00:28:07.719 --> 00:28:11.018
than you're giving
yourself credit for.

00:28:11.089 --> 00:28:15.185
You don't need the collective
to validate your existence.

00:28:15.260 --> 00:28:19.253
You've made an impact
on every member of this crew.

00:28:19.330 --> 00:28:21.230
That's your legacy.

00:28:22.801 --> 00:28:24.098
There you are.

00:28:25.937 --> 00:28:27.564
l should have known
she'd be the one

00:28:27.672 --> 00:28:28.639
to harbor a fugitive.

00:28:28.740 --> 00:28:32.608
We difficult patients
need to stick together.

00:28:32.677 --> 00:28:35.771
l want you to return
to Sick Bay immediately.

00:28:35.847 --> 00:28:37.872
Have you devised
a new treatment?

00:28:37.982 --> 00:28:39.472
Not yet.

00:28:39.551 --> 00:28:41.485
Then it's best
that l don't distract you

00:28:41.553 --> 00:28:42.577
from finding one.

00:28:42.654 --> 00:28:44.781
Seven, if you continue
to exert yourself,

00:28:44.856 --> 00:28:47.586
your condition will
only deteriorate more rapidly.

00:28:47.659 --> 00:28:49.627
ls that what you want?

00:28:49.694 --> 00:28:52.288
What l want is to be useful.

00:28:54.032 --> 00:28:55.363
l really could use her help.

00:28:55.433 --> 00:28:59.164
l promise
not to let her overdo it.

00:29:01.606 --> 00:29:05.736
You can stay, provided
you wear this cortical monitor.

00:29:12.484 --> 00:29:14.577
Thank you.

00:29:36.141 --> 00:29:39.042
Are you feeling better?

00:29:39.110 --> 00:29:41.476
My condition is unchanged.

00:29:45.216 --> 00:29:46.808
l've spoken to the Captain

00:29:46.885 --> 00:29:49.877
about your desire
to apply to Starfleet Academy.

00:29:50.021 --> 00:29:52.854
She's agreed to administer
the entrance exam

00:29:52.924 --> 00:29:57.361
before we send
the next datastream to Earth.

00:29:57.428 --> 00:30:00.886
lt's a list of crewmen
who can help you study.

00:30:01.032 --> 00:30:02.795
Lieutenant Torres is
extremely well-versed

00:30:02.901 --> 00:30:04.198
in warp mechanics.

00:30:04.302 --> 00:30:08.602
Ensign Kim claims to have aced
the quantum theory section.

00:30:08.673 --> 00:30:10.607
What about astrometrics?

00:30:10.675 --> 00:30:16.238
You know more about astrometrics
than most Starfleet officers.

00:30:16.314 --> 00:30:18.509
Still, l'll need someone
to review the material with me.

00:30:18.583 --> 00:30:21.279
l'll ask Lieutenant Paris
to set aside some time.

00:30:21.352 --> 00:30:22.717
l'd rather study with you.

00:30:26.858 --> 00:30:29.156
You've become
too dependent on me.

00:30:29.227 --> 00:30:31.127
You must learn
to rely on others.

00:30:31.196 --> 00:30:32.595
And if l don't want to?

00:30:32.664 --> 00:30:34.256
What you want is irrelevant.

00:30:34.332 --> 00:30:36.163
Why are you acting like this?

00:30:36.267 --> 00:30:38.235
ls it because
you think you're dying?

00:30:38.336 --> 00:30:39.394
l am dying.

00:30:42.674 --> 00:30:45.165
l'm sorry.

00:30:45.276 --> 00:30:49.144
You may have given up,
but l haven't.

00:31:26.451 --> 00:31:28.248
l know how to save her.

00:31:28.319 --> 00:31:30.253
l'm certainly open
to suggestions.

00:31:30.321 --> 00:31:33.222
l've been analyzing
the simulations you performed.

00:31:33.291 --> 00:31:35.759
They failed because
you tried to implement

00:31:35.827 --> 00:31:37.795
a cortical node
from a dead drone.

00:31:37.862 --> 00:31:38.954
That's correct.

00:31:39.030 --> 00:31:40.691
What you require
is a live drone.

00:31:40.765 --> 00:31:43.427
l've already been through that
with Captain Janeway.

00:31:43.534 --> 00:31:45.161
My cortical node is operational.

00:31:45.270 --> 00:31:48.137
l want you to remove it
and give it to Seven.

00:31:48.206 --> 00:31:49.173
Absolutely not!

00:31:49.240 --> 00:31:51.003
Well, at least
review my research.

00:31:51.109 --> 00:31:52.838
lt may as well be
a suicide note.

00:31:52.911 --> 00:31:53.843
l don't agree.

00:31:53.912 --> 00:31:55.004
Well, that's comforting.

00:31:55.146 --> 00:31:57.876
You took these scans of me
when l left the collective.

00:31:57.949 --> 00:31:59.143
By your own estimation,

00:31:59.217 --> 00:32:01.151
l emerged
from my maturation chamber

00:32:01.252 --> 00:32:02.913
before l was fully assimilated.

00:32:03.021 --> 00:32:04.454
As a result, my physiology

00:32:04.522 --> 00:32:06.422
is less dependent
on my implants.

00:32:06.491 --> 00:32:08.891
They still regulate
many of your vital functions.

00:32:08.960 --> 00:32:09.892
What about my age?

00:32:09.961 --> 00:32:11.588
l'm younger, so it
should be easier

00:32:11.663 --> 00:32:13.654
for my body
to adapt to the loss.

00:32:13.731 --> 00:32:14.663
You're obviously too young

00:32:14.732 --> 00:32:15.994
to understand
the risks involved.

00:32:16.067 --> 00:32:17.864
l understand the risks
perfectly.

00:32:17.969 --> 00:32:20.529
lf we continue to do
nothing, Seven will die.

00:32:20.638 --> 00:32:21.605
And if we proceed
with your idea,

00:32:21.706 --> 00:32:22.638
you could both die!

00:32:22.707 --> 00:32:24.106
According to my research,

00:32:24.175 --> 00:32:25.836
there's an 86.9 percent chance

00:32:25.910 --> 00:32:28.401
that Seven's implants
will adapt to my node.

00:32:28.479 --> 00:32:30.106
''Eighty-six...''

00:32:30.181 --> 00:32:31.546
Point nine.

00:32:32.850 --> 00:32:33.942
And what about you?

00:32:34.085 --> 00:32:35.518
Without a cortical node,

00:32:35.586 --> 00:32:37.816
how will you regulate
your implants?

00:32:37.889 --> 00:32:41.347
You should be able to compensate
with genetic resequencing.

00:32:41.426 --> 00:32:43.587
This isn't suicide, Doctor.

00:32:43.661 --> 00:32:45.959
l believe it can work.

00:32:46.097 --> 00:32:48.565
All l ask is that you
consider it.

00:32:56.941 --> 00:32:59.273
Earth's biggest ditch.

00:32:59.344 --> 00:33:01.972
That's what my father
used to call it.

00:33:02.080 --> 00:33:05.072
We hiked the north rim
when l was nine.

00:33:05.116 --> 00:33:07.141
lt's an impressive
geological formation.

00:33:07.218 --> 00:33:10.654
Too dusty. l've always preferred
farm country myself.

00:33:13.591 --> 00:33:16.287
Bloomington, lndiana,
your hometown.

00:33:16.361 --> 00:33:19.819
You've mentioned it
on several occasions.

00:33:19.897 --> 00:33:21.728
So, what do you think?

00:33:21.799 --> 00:33:25.326
lt appears to be
a pleasant environment.

00:33:25.436 --> 00:33:28.030
When we get to Earth,
l'll take you there.

00:33:28.139 --> 00:33:29.071
lt's more likely

00:33:29.140 --> 00:33:31.301
this crew will reach Earth
without me.

00:33:31.376 --> 00:33:33.674
You don't know that.

00:33:33.745 --> 00:33:37.943
You refuse to acknowledge
the severity of my condition,

00:33:38.049 --> 00:33:39.846
just as l did at first.

00:33:39.917 --> 00:33:42.852
Are you giving up?

00:33:42.920 --> 00:33:45.514
l'm merely accepting reality.

00:33:46.591 --> 00:33:49.890
lf l'd accepted reality
six years ago,

00:33:49.961 --> 00:33:52.054
l'd have settled
on the first M-Class planet

00:33:52.130 --> 00:33:53.062
we came across.

00:33:53.131 --> 00:33:55.463
lnstead, l'm 30,000
light-years closer

00:33:55.533 --> 00:33:56.966
to Bloomington, lndiana.

00:33:57.101 --> 00:33:59.296
Minus several members
of your crew.

00:34:00.972 --> 00:34:04.169
Ensign Marie Kaplan,

00:34:04.242 --> 00:34:07.040
Ensign Lyndsay Ballard,
Crewman Timothy Lang...

00:34:07.111 --> 00:34:08.601
ls there a point to this?

00:34:08.679 --> 00:34:12.171
Every person on this list
died under your command.

00:34:12.250 --> 00:34:15.083
You accepted their deaths,

00:34:15.153 --> 00:34:18.350
but l don't believe
you'll accept mine.

00:34:18.423 --> 00:34:20.118
That's presumptuous.

00:34:20.191 --> 00:34:21.886
l'm not being egotistical.

00:34:21.959 --> 00:34:24.826
On the contrary,
l'm trying to make a point.

00:34:24.896 --> 00:34:26.363
Which is?

00:34:28.666 --> 00:34:32.534
All of these crew members
came to Voyager

00:34:32.637 --> 00:34:35.105
with unique personalities,

00:34:35.206 --> 00:34:37.800
but l have required
your constant assistance

00:34:37.909 --> 00:34:39.706
to develop my individuality.

00:34:39.777 --> 00:34:41.438
And you've come a long way.

00:34:41.512 --> 00:34:42.672
But not far enough.

00:34:42.747 --> 00:34:45.841
l've disappointed you.

00:34:45.917 --> 00:34:48.750
You feel your task
is incomplete.

00:34:48.820 --> 00:34:51.880
That's why my death will be
difficult for you to accept.

00:34:51.956 --> 00:34:54.288
ls that what you think?

00:34:54.358 --> 00:34:58.920
That you haven't lived up
to my expectations?

00:34:58.996 --> 00:35:00.896
Clearly, l haven't,

00:35:00.998 --> 00:35:03.466
but l want you to know

00:35:03.568 --> 00:35:08.198
that the failure
has been mine, not yours.

00:35:09.307 --> 00:35:13.073
You haven't failed, Seven.

00:35:13.144 --> 00:35:16.136
You've exceeded my expectations.

00:35:16.214 --> 00:35:17.875
You've become an individual,

00:35:17.982 --> 00:35:19.882
an extraordinary individual.

00:35:20.017 --> 00:35:23.248
lf l'm having trouble
accepting your condition,

00:35:23.321 --> 00:35:27.621
it's only because l don't
want to lose a friend.

00:35:29.827 --> 00:35:31.454
Doctor to the Captain.
l need to see you

00:35:31.529 --> 00:35:33.827
and Seven right away.

00:35:36.167 --> 00:35:38.465
lt would be
a complicated procedure.

00:35:38.569 --> 00:35:39.501
No doubt.

00:35:39.570 --> 00:35:41.128
But you believe it'll work.

00:35:41.239 --> 00:35:43.639
There are significant
risks involved...

00:35:43.708 --> 00:35:44.800
to Seven and lcheb,

00:35:44.909 --> 00:35:46.900
but if you're asking
me if it's possible,

00:35:47.011 --> 00:35:48.035
l'd have to say yes.

00:35:48.112 --> 00:35:49.204
What sort of precautions...?

00:35:49.280 --> 00:35:50.770
No matter how many
precautions you take,

00:35:50.848 --> 00:35:52.145
it's not worth
the risk to lcheb.

00:35:52.216 --> 00:35:53.274
Seven, this could work.

00:35:53.351 --> 00:35:54.682
l'm not willing
to extend my life

00:35:54.752 --> 00:35:55.946
at the cost of yours.

00:35:56.087 --> 00:35:57.952
But you haven't
reviewed all the data.

00:35:58.022 --> 00:35:59.751
As long as there is any chance

00:35:59.824 --> 00:36:02.224
you won't survive,
the data is irrelevant.

00:36:02.326 --> 00:36:04.385
l'd like to return
to Sick Bay now.

00:36:04.428 --> 00:36:06.157
As you wish.

00:36:10.401 --> 00:36:11.459
You're the Captain.

00:36:11.569 --> 00:36:13.196
You could order her to do it.

00:36:13.304 --> 00:36:15.204
l have to respect her wishes.

00:36:15.273 --> 00:36:16.672
Even if it kills her?

00:36:16.741 --> 00:36:19.574
l want to help her
just as much as you do.

00:36:19.644 --> 00:36:23.307
lf that were true,
you wouldn't let her die.

00:36:33.858 --> 00:36:36.884
ls there anything l can bring
from the Cargo Bay

00:36:37.028 --> 00:36:38.893
to make you feel more at home?

00:36:39.030 --> 00:36:40.088
No, thank you.

00:36:40.164 --> 00:36:42.496
Something from the Mess Hall?

00:36:42.567 --> 00:36:43.898
A piece of fruit?

00:36:44.001 --> 00:36:46.731
Are you offering me
my last meal?

00:36:46.837 --> 00:36:48.828
l... o-of course not.

00:36:48.940 --> 00:36:50.635
ls that what you thought?

00:36:50.708 --> 00:36:53.472
l was attempting
to lighten the mood.

00:36:53.544 --> 00:36:56.069
Ah, yes.
Well done.

00:36:56.147 --> 00:36:57.580
lcheb to the Doctor.

00:36:57.648 --> 00:37:00.208
Report to Cargo Bay 2
immediately.

00:37:00.284 --> 00:37:01.546
He's persistent.

00:37:01.619 --> 00:37:03.211
Not to worry.

00:37:03.287 --> 00:37:07.053
l'll make it clear to him
that persistence is futile.

00:37:14.332 --> 00:37:16.926
You were summoned, too?

00:37:17.034 --> 00:37:19.127
lcheb doesn't seem
to have grasped

00:37:19.237 --> 00:37:20.761
the chain of command yet.

00:37:20.871 --> 00:37:23.704
Remind you of anyone we know?

00:37:23.774 --> 00:37:25.105
lcheb!

00:37:30.681 --> 00:37:32.876
He's disengaged
his cortical node!

00:37:32.984 --> 00:37:33.973
How?

00:37:34.051 --> 00:37:35.075
My alcove...

00:37:35.152 --> 00:37:37.643
l programmed it
to disconnect my neural relays.

00:37:37.722 --> 00:37:38.814
Can you reconnect them?

00:37:38.889 --> 00:37:40.686
He's locked me out
of the controls.

00:37:40.758 --> 00:37:41.850
How could you do this?

00:37:41.926 --> 00:37:44.053
lt was the only way
l could prove to you

00:37:44.128 --> 00:37:45.186
that it would work.

00:37:58.809 --> 00:37:59.935
What's wrong with him?

00:38:00.011 --> 00:38:02.206
lcheb decided to perform
a little operation

00:38:02.246 --> 00:38:03.372
on himself.

00:38:03.414 --> 00:38:05.746
You have to reconnect
his node immediately.

00:38:05.816 --> 00:38:07.078
l intend to.

00:38:07.151 --> 00:38:09.745
No. lf Seven can refuse
treatment, so can l.

00:38:09.820 --> 00:38:10.980
We don't have time for this.

00:38:11.055 --> 00:38:12.283
Well, then, check your scans.

00:38:12.356 --> 00:38:13.687
You'll see l'm already adapting.

00:38:13.758 --> 00:38:15.817
Some of your implants
have adapted, but not all.

00:38:15.926 --> 00:38:17.826
Then apply the resequencing
technique l researched.

00:38:17.962 --> 00:38:19.395
This debate is pointless.

00:38:19.463 --> 00:38:20.828
l won't accept the node.

00:38:20.931 --> 00:38:22.455
And l won't keep it.

00:38:22.533 --> 00:38:24.057
Someone had better
use the damn thing.

00:38:24.168 --> 00:38:25.635
lf it stays
disconnected much longer,

00:38:25.736 --> 00:38:27.169
it won't do either
of you any good.

00:38:27.238 --> 00:38:29.172
You're acting like a child.

00:38:29.240 --> 00:38:30.673
l'm trying to save your life.

00:38:30.741 --> 00:38:32.709
Only because you've grown
too dependent on me.

00:38:32.777 --> 00:38:34.972
So you think l need to learn
to rely on other people?

00:38:35.046 --> 00:38:36.070
-Yes.
-What about you?

00:38:36.147 --> 00:38:39.514
You've refused to rely
on a single member of this crew.

00:38:39.583 --> 00:38:41.608
You hid your condition
from the rest of us.

00:38:41.686 --> 00:38:42.880
You deactivated the Doctor,

00:38:42.987 --> 00:38:45.387
and now
you're rejecting my help.

00:38:45.456 --> 00:38:47.856
You're the one who needs
to rely on others.

00:38:47.925 --> 00:38:50.018
lsn't that what people
on this ship do?

00:38:50.094 --> 00:38:51.220
They help each other?

00:38:51.295 --> 00:38:52.353
Whenever we can.

00:38:52.430 --> 00:38:55.228
lf the Captain were dying,

00:38:55.299 --> 00:38:57.563
you'd risk your life to
save her, wouldn't you?

00:38:57.668 --> 00:38:59.067
And when you respond
to a distress call,

00:38:59.136 --> 00:39:01.036
you're risking the life
of everyone on this ship

00:39:01.138 --> 00:39:04.198
to respond to the aid
of strangers.

00:39:04.308 --> 00:39:05.866
He's right.

00:39:05.976 --> 00:39:08.570
Captain, he's just a child.

00:39:08.646 --> 00:39:11.012
l don't think he is...

00:39:11.082 --> 00:39:13.016
not anymore.

00:39:13.084 --> 00:39:14.711
Doctor.

00:39:14.785 --> 00:39:17.413
Don't look at me.

00:39:17.488 --> 00:39:19.683
Please.

00:39:19.757 --> 00:39:21.622
Just let us help you.

00:39:37.942 --> 00:39:39.967
Let's begin.

00:41:11.569 --> 00:41:13.730
Good morning.

00:41:13.838 --> 00:41:16.136
How long have l
been regenerating?

00:41:16.207 --> 00:41:17.299
Six days.

00:41:17.408 --> 00:41:19.308
We needed to make sure
your implants

00:41:19.376 --> 00:41:21.469
had completely adapted
to the new node.

00:41:21.545 --> 00:41:23.638
The good news is they have.

00:41:26.550 --> 00:41:27.642
lcheb.

00:41:30.888 --> 00:41:31.946
His road to recovery

00:41:32.089 --> 00:41:34.489
has been a little bumpier
than yours.

00:41:34.558 --> 00:41:37.493
Has he suffered
any permanent damage?

00:41:37.561 --> 00:41:38.823
l don't think so.

00:41:38.896 --> 00:41:41.228
He's been experiencing
some pain,

00:41:41.298 --> 00:41:43.391
but l believe it's temporary.

00:41:43.467 --> 00:41:44.832
Pain l caused him.

00:41:44.935 --> 00:41:47.495
Pain he was willing to endure.

00:42:04.488 --> 00:42:05.750
You've recovered.

00:42:05.823 --> 00:42:08.383
l expect the same from you.

00:42:08.459 --> 00:42:12.589
The Doctor wants
to keep me here another week,

00:42:12.663 --> 00:42:17.760
but l'm sure l'll be back
on my feet in half that time.

00:42:17.868 --> 00:42:21.031
l suggest you get
as much rest as you can.

00:42:21.138 --> 00:42:22.935
You're going to need it.

00:42:23.073 --> 00:42:24.938
Why?

00:42:25.075 --> 00:42:27.339
l've decided
to help you prepare

00:42:27.411 --> 00:42:30.938
for the astrometrics portion
of the Academy exam.

00:42:31.048 --> 00:42:34.506
You can expect a rigorous
and grueling schedule.

00:42:38.556 --> 00:42:40.148
Seven...

00:42:40.224 --> 00:42:41.486
Yes.

00:42:41.559 --> 00:42:43.652
Your ocular implant--

00:42:43.727 --> 00:42:46.025
it's malfunctioning again.

00:42:51.201 --> 00:42:52.429
Actually...

00:42:52.536 --> 00:42:54.663
it's functioning perfectly.
